{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560067-mage-story-with-a-new-council-of-nine","id":1560067,"title":"Mage story with a new Council of Nine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-18T11:41:45-07:00","id":1560067,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Mage story with a new Council of Nine","content":"I've started working on an idea for a story with a new Council of Nine. Basically there's going to be a major global catastrophe that will decimate the world's mages. It makes the war between the Council of Nine and the Technocracy irrelevant since there are new, more pressing threats. The world will sort of be lightly post-apocalyptic - as far as sleepers are concerned, the world just went through major, devastating disasters that they don't really understand, but life is now returning to normal, despite mass casualties. Following the disasters, the Nephandi have gained a major foothold and their power and influence are growing to a level they've never experienced before. Their influence over sleepers is also growing via companies like Pentex, corrupt governments, and manipulative religious leaders.<br /> <br /> The catastrophe affected different magical groups to different extents, wiping some out, while others carry on. The new council is as follows:<br /> <b>Dissonance Society</b> - Time (these radical Ecstatics were able to mobilize as radicals and survivalists, weathering the catastrophe better than the rest of the Cult of Ecstasy)<br /> <b>Mo-Tzu Fa</b> - Mind (these Li Hai were not hit as hard as the rest of the Akashic Brotherhood because of their deep integration with sleeper society and their focus on pragmatism)<br /> <b>Hollow Ones</b> - Prime (because of their individualism they weathered the storm very well)<br /> <b>Psychopharmacopoeists</b> - Life (their drugs and medications helped them and others survive, although other Progenitors were less fortunate)<br /> <b>Lifeweavers</b> - Entropy (like others, their individuality helped them weather the storm, but other Verbena were more vulnerable)<br /> <b>Kahin</b> - Forces (the Zaotar threw themselves into facing the catastrophe and ensuing conflicts, which basically wiped them out, but the Kahin survived because they're just as strong as other Taft\u00e2ni, they live in remote desert, they're more subtle/covert)<br /> <b>Darwushim</b> - Correspondence (the Ahl-i-Batin survived the catastrophe particularly well, and following it the Darwushim assumed a leadership role)<br /> <b>BioMechanics</b> - Matter (they altered themselves with technology, which facilitated their survival, but they're the only part of the Iteration X doing particularly well)<br /> <b>Sons of Tengri</b> - Spirit (their independent spirit and their location in remote rural Mongolia helped them evade the catastrophe better than other shamanic mages)<br /> <br /> Note these explanations are all post-hoc - in reality these are just groups I like, that I'd like to use.<br /> <br /> There's also a new antagonist. The <b>Templar Knights</b> and the <b>Septarians</b> of the Celestial Chorus are convinced that the catastrophe was God's judgment, so they come together to form an especially brutal new group that wants to wipe out other mage groups for provoking God's wrath. This group would be somewhere between a modern <b>Cabal of Pure Thought,</b> the Magisterium from His Dark Materials, and a survivalist militia.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12725-amebix","name":"Amebix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T13:22:14-07:00","id":1560074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amebix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560067-mage-story-with-a-new-council-of-nine#post1560067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Always fun to see people come up with radically different Traditions.<br /> <br /> I'm curious if you're thinking that these groups are more or less the pre-apocalypse groups, or whether they've absorbed other mages?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Psychopharmacopoeists</b> - Life (their drugs and medications helped them and others survive, although other Progenitors were less fortunate) </div> </div> </div>Just for clarity, why did you go for a micro-methodology and not their parent Pharmacopoeists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T13:39:55-07:00","id":1560075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560067-mage-story-with-a-new-council-of-nine?p=1560074#post1560074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Always fun to see people come up with radically different Traditions.<br /> <br /> I'm curious if you're thinking that these groups are more or less the pre-apocalypse groups, or whether they've absorbed other mages?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Just for clarity, why did you go for a micro-methodology and not their parent Pharmacopoeists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I definitely think there would be some shuffling. It would probably be better to go for the general Pharmacopoeists, but I want particular emphasis on psychiatric drugs because I think it's just a lot more interesting for how they would enhance the mages' abilities. And I definitely think there would be some absorption and reshuffling going on with the different groups. I'm thinking these sects would become the dominant forces of their old traditions/crafts/conventions, but things wouldn't work out totally cleanly. I would imagine the Syndicate and remaining Void Engineers would be small independent groups, and I don't really see any room for the NWO in this world, so maybe former NWO operatives would become enforcers for the Syndicate as it tries to regain some power. I would think the members of the other Ecstatic and Akashic sects would take cues from the Dissonance Society and Mo-Tzu Fa, respectively, in becoming more pragmatic and modernizing some of their methods, and I could see other Verbena learning the Lifeweavers' methods.<br /> <br /> The group I feel the shakiest with is the Sons of Tengri, and I almost gave Spirit to the Bata'a. I'm not really sure, maybe I should formulate my own alternative to the Dreamspeakers that would be globally inclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12725,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12725-amebix","user":"Amebix","date":". 05-18-2026, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12725-amebix","name":"Amebix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T14:05:15-07:00","id":1560076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amebix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560067-mage-story-with-a-new-council-of-nine?p=1560075#post1560075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I definitely think there would be some absorption and reshuffling going on with the different groups. I'm thinking these sects would become the dominant forces of their old traditions/crafts/conventions, but things wouldn't work out totally cleanly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first people to come to my mind were the Children of Knowledge. They could make an interesting mix with an ex-Progenitor methodology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The group I feel the shakiest with is the Sons of Tengri, and I almost gave Spirit to the Bata'a. I'm not really sure, maybe I should formulate my own alternative to the Dreamspeakers that would be globally inclusive. </div> </div> </div>The Bata'a are probably a more coherent option, though honestly, the SoT are such a wild card to go for, I kinda like it.<br /> <br /> I suppose the trouble is that from the sounds of it, they've survived due to their remoteness rather than their pragmatism which perhaps implies they'd have less to teach other mages?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T14:18:57-07:00","id":1560077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560067-mage-story-with-a-new-council-of-nine?p=1560076#post1560076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first people to come to my mind were the Children of Knowledge. They could make an interesting mix with an ex-Progenitor methodology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that idea! Especially considering their association with psychedelics, they'd be perfect for this version of the Psychopharmacopoeists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12725-amebix","name":"Amebix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T14:41:43-07:00","id":1560079,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit confused as to the narrative logic of why certain groups succeeded and others failed to adapt to the catastrophe and its aftermath; perhaps because a lot of the event itself is currently undefined. It also seems odd that there would be a reason for these groups to form some sort of new alliance based on how much there seems to be a separatist/isolationist bend to many of the groups listed. For example the Kahin (who are Spirit focused, not Forces focused...) surviving while the Zaotar didn't doesn't really change that the Kahin were just as uncaring about being part of a wider alliance as a group before the M20 metaplot created an internal generational change in the Taftani that lead to both factions being less isolationist and more cooperative with outside groups that makes them a viable option to join the Disparates. But that means the cooperative Taftani weren't out in the isolated desert and insulated from the events in this new timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}